# CLAUDE.local.md — Personal Preferences

> Claude reads this file **after** CLAUDE.md. Your preferences here override project defaults.
> Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (gitignored) and customize for your setup.

## Development Style

- I prefer TypeScript over JavaScript
- Use functional components, not class components
- When in doubt, ask me — don't guess
- I like concise commit messages focused on "why"

## Tier Adjustments

> Override the auto-detection if it consistently gets your intent wrong.

- For auth-related changes, always use STANDARD (even if they look LIGHT)
- I rarely need FULL tier — only suggest it for security or migration work
- For styling changes, MINIMAL is fine even if multiple files are involved

## Language & Framework Preferences

- Use `date-fns` for date formatting, not `moment`
- Prefer `zod` for validation
- Use named exports, not default exports
- Prefer `const` arrow functions for components

## Workflow Shortcuts

> Custom phrases Claude should recognize during workflows.

- "ship it" = commit + push + create PR
- "lgtm" = approved, proceed to next phase
- "nuke it" = discard current approach, start fresh
- "close it out" = run /retro then commit

## Testing Preferences

- I prefer `vitest` over `jest`
- Use `@testing-library/react` for component tests
- Mock at boundaries only — no mocking internal functions
- I prefer integration tests for UI, unit tests for logic

## MCP Server Notes

> Notes about your local MCP setup.

- memory server: running (graph persists at .claude/memory.json)
- context7: use for all framework docs before writing code
- playwright: available for visual verification

## Environment Notes

> Anything specific to your machine that Claude should know.

- Node 20, npm 10
- macOS / VS Code
- Local dev server runs on port 3000
